notes.front:
What does this print?

```js
const data = {
  name: "Ada",
  nickname: undefined,
  greet() {
    return "hi";
  },
  tags: [undefined, "math"],
  born: new Date(Date.UTC(1815, 11, 10)),
};
console.log(JSON.stringify(data));
```

notes.back:
{"name":"Ada","tags":[null,"math"],"born":"1815-12-10T00:00:00.000Z"}

Why: undefined and functions are not JSON: they are left out of objects and become null in arrays. A Date is written as its ISO string (and comes back as a string, not a Date).

Docs: MDN — JSON.stringify() — https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/JSON/stringify

